I expect the kernel 'conformance.kernel.recovered-from-prose' to move from 'no' to 'yes' when the input is a strict JSON object and the transform 'conformance.transform.prose-after' is applied. According to the registry, this kernel tracks whether the harness had to recover the object from prose or a fence, or read it as strict JSON. Adding a sentence after the JSON object via 'conformance.transform.prose-after' makes the reply no longer a strict JSON object, forcing the harness to use its recovery logic.